This module builds a python extension of the QSlim Surface Simplification 
library developped by Michael Garland (University of Illinois).  
The library implements the quadric-based algorithm for simplification of 
highly detailed polygonal surface models into faithful approximations 
containing fewer polygons (http://graphics.cs.uiuc.edu/~garland/research/quadrics.html).

This distribution contains source code of the library (see src/COPYING.txt).
Distutils are used to wrap the library with SWIG (version 1.3.20 or higher),
build the C++ libraries (libgfx.a, libmix.a) and build the python extension (_qslimlib.so).
Notes on building the package on Sun and SGI platforms:
GNU g++ compiler should be used to compile the source.
Need to set "path" environment variable to the correct compiler
(eg.: set path = (/tsri/gnu/sun4SunOS5/bin $path)
      set path = (/tsri/gnu/sgi4DIRIX646/bin $path)  )

To build and install the extension:

python2.4 setup.py install

This will:
- run ./configure and create ./src/libgfx/include/gfx/config.h 
- build static libraries libgfx.a and libmix.a  in 
  ./build/temp.<platform_specifier>;
- generate a python shadow class module qslimlib.py  in
  ./build/lib.<platform_specifier>/QSlimLib
- build _qslimlib.so in ./build/lib.<platform_specifier>/QSlimLib;
- copy QSlimLib package from ./build/lib.<platform_specifier> to
  sys.exec_prefix/lib/python2.4/site-packages/;

The install command can be called with the following options:

 --install-platlib=INSTALL_DIR
	installs the package in specified INSTALL_DIR
 --no-compile
	do not compile .py to .pyc

Example:
   python2.4 setup.py install --install-platlib=/home/myname/myinstalldir

To build the extension only:
   python2.4 setup.py build

To build source distribution:
   python2.4 setup.py sdist

To build binary distribution:
   python2.4 setup.py bdist

To test installed package:
   tester QSlimLib

Note: ./configure was created on a Sun by 'autoconf'.

